#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# region_measure

#% text
# `region_measure(reg)` is the measure of the region in its own dimension: the length of a curve, the area of a surface, the volume of a solid; for finitely many points, their number (the counting measure).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact coordinates give exact results; symbolic ones give formulas.

#% item
# A degenerate primitive is the set it actually is: a triangle with equal or collinear corners is the segment between its outermost corners, a tetrahedron with coplanar corners the convex polygon they span, a polygon whose corners lie on one line a segment, a line with equal ends, or a disk, ball, circle or sphere of radius 0, a point. Its measure is the one of the dimension it has: `area` and `volume` of a lower-dimensional region are 0.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A disk and a ball of radius r:

#% cell
[region_measure(disk([0, 0], r)), region_measure(ball([0, 0, 0], r))]
#% output
#= [pi*r^2, (4/3)*pi*r^3]

#% text
# A polyline:

#% cell
region_measure(line([[0, 0], [1, 1], [1, 0]]))
#% output
#= 1 + 2^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A triangle with two equal corners is a segment, a disk of radius 0 a point:

#% cell
[region_measure(triangle([[0, 0], [1, 1], [1, 1]])), area(triangle([[0, 0], [1, 1], [1, 1]])), region_measure(disk([1, 2], 0))]
#% output
#= [2^(1/2), 0, 1]

#% text
# An ellipse's area:

#% cell
region_measure(disk([0, 0], [2, 3]))
#% output
#= 6*pi

#% text
# A rectangle with symbolic corners:

#% cell
region_measure(rectangle([a, b], [c, d]))
#% output
#= abs((c - a)*(d - b))

#% text
# A circle's length and a sphere's area:

#% cell
[region_measure(circle()), region_measure(sphere())]
#% output
#= [2*pi, 4*pi]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `area`, `volume`, `arc_length`, `region_centroid`
